# Git — per-host clone (July 2026 VM split)

## Policy

Repos are moving to **dedicated VMs** (100 ALFA-AI, 102 MARKET, 103 ATEMS, etc.). The old rule — **commit/push only from `apps`** — is **retired**.

**Each host that owns a repo clone** may run the full git loop locally:

| Step | Where |
|------|--------|
| Edit code / docs | The host that owns the checkout (or agent workspace on that host) |
| `git commit` | Same host |
| `git push origin main` | Same host |
| `git pull --ff-only` | Every **other** clone of that repo before deploy |

Never `git pull` on the host that **just pushed** in the same session ([git-no-pull-on-push-host.mdc](git-no-pull-on-push-host.mdc)).

**GitHub** (`origin`) is the sync bus — not SCP between hosts.

## Host → repo ownership (examples)

| Host | Typical clone path | Repos |
|------|-------------------|-------|
| **`pool_opt_in`** | `/home/operator/alfa-ai` | `alfa-ai` (pool27 shard `:31354`) |
| **`rag`** | `/home/operator/alfa-ai` | `alfa-ai` (CPU RAG staging / cutover target) |
| **`apps`** | `/home/ansible/<repo>` | Remaining apps on 105 + sibling repos still colocated |
| **`orchestrator`** | `C:\Users\operator\alfa-ai` | `alfa-ai` (Windows dev / orchestrator) |
| **`market`** | `/home/ansible/market-pie5-bot` | `market-pie5-bot` |
| **`atems`** | `/home/operator/atems` | `atems` |
| **`monitor`** | `/home/ansible/monitoring` | `monitoring` |
| **`hub`** | `/mnt/HDDs/Alfa-AI/repo/alfa-ai` | `alfa-ai` (hub clone — pull only until brain moves) |

A change to **repo X** is committed and pushed from the host that **runs** repo X (or where the agent is actively editing). Other hosts **pull** before deploy.

## Agent workflow

1. **Research + docs** per [doc-first-development.mdc](doc-first-development.mdc).
2. **Edit** in the active workspace (`orchestrator`, `apps`, `pool_opt_in` SSH, etc.).
3. **`git commit`** from that workspace — include docs + code in one commit when both changed.
4. **Pre-commit** when `deploy/` changed: `pwsh -NoProfile -File deploy/cluster-members/_common/Test-AlfaPowerShellScriptSyntax.ps1 -Recurse deploy`
5. **`git push origin main`** from the same host.
6. **`git pull --ff-only`** on every other clone before deploy on that host.
7. **Deploy** per [cluster-sync-order.mdc](cluster-sync-order.mdc).

## Multi-repo / mapping file sync

`docs/REPO_HOST_MAPPING.md` master copy lives in **alfa-ai**. After editing:

- Commit/push **alfa-ai** from the host doing the edit (`orchestrator`, `apps`, or `pool_opt_in`).
- Propagate the file to sibling repos (`scripts/sync-repo-host-mapping.sh` or manual `cp`).
- Commit/push **each sibling repo from the host that owns that clone** (`apps` for repos still there; `market` for market-bot; etc.).

## Never commit

- Live `.env`, secrets, operator-only tokens ([secrets-and-env.mdc](secrets-and-env.mdc)).
- `tmp-*` scratch files unless explicitly part of the deliverable.

## `hub` and gaming workers

Operator runs `git pull` on `hub` and workers — agents do not SSH-commit there ([cluster-host-command-execution.mdc](cluster-host-command-execution.mdc)).

